Subject: [PATCH] a module can steer a bot's loot roll vote

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

mod-overseer runs a loot council for the families it drives: a drop goes to
whoever in the family it upgrades most, then to the guild's raiders, the way a
guild hands loot out. For a party on need before greed that means the council's
recipient needs and everybody else passes. The vote is cast here, and nowhere
else can reach it first.

mod-overseer's own comment on its removed need vote (mod_overseer.cpp, "WHY THIS
DRIVE CASTS NO NEED/GREED VOTE") has the measurement: LootRollAction answers a
roll from the SMSG_LOOT_START_ROLL packet, at relevance 100, and votes on every
roll where its own vote is still NOT_EMITED_YET. World::Update runs every bot's
AI before the module's OnUpdate, and Group::GroupLoot sends the packet before
it pushes the roll onto RollId, so no poll and no packet hook in the module can
act before this action does. That comment names this file as where the rule has
to live.

THE CHANGE

A steer a module installs once at startup with SetLootRollSteer. For each open
roll the bot has not voted on, Execute asks it first:

  - false: the steer has no opinion, and the upstream rule votes as before.
  - true with a vote: that vote is cast through Group::CountRollVote.
  - true with NOT_EMITED_YET: nothing is cast this time. The vote stays
    NOT_EMITED_YET, so the next Execute (the module calls this action from its
    own drive every few seconds) asks again.

The steer is one function pointer, set before any bot votes and only read
afterwards. It is held in a std::atomic (release on the store, acquire on
every read) so the map threads that read it agree with the startup that wrote
it without relying on thread start order; whatever the module keeps behind it
is the module's to guard.

A steer that holds too long costs a pass: Group::EndRoll counts a vote never
cast as a pass when the sixty seconds run out. mod-overseer's steer returns
false after 45 seconds (LOOT_COUNCIL_ROLL_LAST_SECONDS) for exactly that reason.

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CHANGE

The upstream rule, including 0008's greed on BAD_EQUIP, for every bot the
steer returns false for: every bot on a realm without mod-overseer, every bot
outside a family's party, and every item that is not a weapon or armour.
MasterLootRollAction and RollAction are untouched.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream offering a script hook ahead of the bot's roll vote.

APPLIES TO

mod-playerbots @ 8d9f6aa6bc6d45f9ae0ee0675b9b1f8aa6937312, on top of local
patches 0001-0014. Touches only LootRollAction.h and LootRollAction::Execute.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootRollAction.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootRollAction.cpp
index 4737d63..e22aa29 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootRollAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootRollAction.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,15 @@
 #include "PlayerbotAIConfig.h"
 #include "Playerbots.h"
 
+#include <atomic>
+
+// infra: see SetLootRollSteer in LootRollAction.h. Set once at startup, before
+// any bot votes, and read from every map thread afterwards; atomic, so the
+// write and every read agree without relying on when the threads started.
+static std::atomic<LootRollSteer> sLootRollSteer{nullptr};
+
+void SetLootRollSteer(LootRollSteer steer) { sLootRollSteer.store(steer, std::memory_order_release); }
+
 bool LootRollAction::Execute(Event /*event*/)
 {
     Group* group = bot->GetGroup();
@@ -27,6 +36,19 @@ bool LootRollAction::Execute(Event /*event*/)
         if (voteItr == roll->playerVote.end() || voteItr->second != NOT_EMITED_YET)
             continue;
 
+        // infra: a module's decision comes first. NOT_EMITED_YET holds the
+        // vote, so the roll stays open for this bot until the steer decides.
+        LootRollSteer const steer = sLootRollSteer.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+        RollVote steered = NOT_EMITED_YET;
+        if (steer && steer(bot, roll, steered))
+        {
+            if (steered == NOT_EMITED_YET)
+                continue;
+            group->CountRollVote(bot->GetGUID(), roll->itemGUID, steered);
+            voted = true;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         ObjectGuid guid = roll->itemGUID;
         uint32 itemId = roll->itemid;
         int32 randomProperty = 0;
